<title>USA: Mercantile Stores Q1 shr $0.52 vs $0.36.</title>
<headline>Mercantile Stores Q1 shr $0.52 vs $0.36.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFIELD, Ohio 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>MERCANTILE STORES COMPANY, INC.</p>
<p>			  First Quarter Results</p>
<p>For the Thirteen Weeks Ended May 3, 1997 and May 4, 1996</p>
<p>						  Thirteen Weeks Ended</p>
<p> (unaudited, in thousands)     May 3, 1997	  May 4, 1996</p>
<p> except per share data)	 ____________	 ____________</p>
<p> Total Revenues		    $   683,298	  $   655,409</p>
<p>Cost, Expenses and Other Income:</p>
<p>Cost of Goods Sold (including</p>
<p>occupancy and central buying</p>
<p>   expenses)			     478,928		452,969</p>
<p>Selling, General and</p>
<p> Administrative Expenses	     172,642		168,251</p>
<p> Interest Expense, net		   3,235		  2,414</p>
<p> Other Income			    (3,252)		(2,314)</p>
<p> Impairment Charge			     -		 12,000</p>
<p>					     651,553		633,320</p>
<p> Income before Income Taxes	   31,745		 22,089</p>
<p> Income Taxes			     12,437		  8,818</p>
<p> Net Income				 19,308		 13,271</p>
<p> Net Income per Share			.52		    .36</p>
<p>NOTE:  (A)  The 1996 quarter reflects a pre-tax charge totaling</p>
<p>	   $12 million, or $ .20 per share, attributable to the</p>
<p>	   adoption of a new accounting standard related to the</p>
<p>		 impairment of long-lived assets.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
